Package: LeadTime
Type: Package
Title: R package for lead time bias estimation and correction in cancer screening studies
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Marius Robert
Maintainer: Marius Robert <marius.robert@u-bordeaux.fr>
Description: LeadTime is a package designed to analyze cancer screening data and estimate lead time bias. This bias is due to the difference in temporality between a diagnosis by screening and a diagnosis by symptoms. Consequently, the observed post-diagnosis survival is overestimated for patients detected by screening compared to those detected by symptoms. The cause is that the survival times compared have different starting points in the natural history of the disease because screening always takes place before the appearance of symptoms. The longer survival observed in patients is partly due to the benefit of early detection of cancer but is also artificially extended by lead time bias.
